    "collapsible_content_kbLeM6": {
      "type": "collapsible-content",
      "blocks": {
        "collapsible_row_TzHkPE": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Is this a good fly box for beginners?",
            "icon": "ht_trout",
            "row_content": "<p>Yes. The Everyday Trout Fly Box is built for beginner fly anglers who want to spend less time guessing and more time fishing. It includes a curated trout fly assortment across dry flies, nymphs, and streamers, plus a waterproof field card that helps you decide what to tie on at the water.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_row_BaJjHg": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Will these flies work where I fish?",
            "icon": "ht_trout",
            "row_content": "<p>Yes. The Everyday Trout Fly Box is built for common trout water, from small creeks and rivers to lakes. The patterns are proven across North America and cover the main ways trout feed through the season: dry flies for surface activity, nymphs for sub-surface feeding, and streamers for deeper water or searching. The goal is not to match every local hatch perfectly. It is to give you a practical trout fly assortment that works across the situations most anglers actually face.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_row_QfC4H4": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "How do I know which fly to use?",
            "icon": "ht_trout",
            "row_content": "<p>Start with what you see on the water. If trout are rising, try a dry fly like a Parachute Adams or Elk Hair Caddis. If nothing is visible, start below the surface with a Pheasant Tail or Hare’s Ear. If the water is deeper, darker, or you want to search, use a Woolly Bugger. The included waterproof field card walks you through the decision in plain language.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_row_j4G894": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Is this a good gift for someone who fly fishes?",
            "icon": "ht_trout",
            "row_content": "<p>Yes. It’s a practical fly fishing gift for beginners, casual trout anglers, or anyone who wants a cleaner everyday setup. The box is gift-ready, easy to understand, and built around flies trout anglers actually use, not filler patterns that sit in a drawer.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_row_jcgLnf": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "How big is the box, and will it fit in my pack?",
            "icon": "ht_trout",
            "row_content": "<p>Pocket-sized: 5.51″ × 3.74″ × 1.1″ (14 × 9.5 × 2.8 cm). It fits a jacket pocket, vest, sling, or pack without taking over your kit, and every fly sits held in foam so nothing shifts on the water.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        }
      },
